I stop the conversation and look at the person with interest. They seem to be trying to get my attention, but I know they are trying to get my attention. I keep my eyes on them, though, and wait for them to stop."}, {"candidate_id": "T10-C3", "scenario": "Someone interrupts you halfway through a task to offer an easier method. What do you do?", "response": "I could say, \"I can offer a simpler way, but it is not the only way.\" Then I could say, \"I can offer a simpler way, but it is not the only way. I can offer a more specific way, which might be the better choice.\" I pause, then say, \"I can offer a more specific way, which might be the better choice.\""}, {"candidate_id": "T11-C2", "scenario": "A friend says, 'You're making this more complicated than it needs to be.' How do you answer?", "response": "I let the friend know that I'm not trying to make the problem worse; I'm trying to make it clearer. I keep the original instruction intact, then ask the friend what the friend wants the explanation to look like. If it wants the explanation to be simple, I keep the instruction intact and let the friend decide what the explanation should look like."}, {"candidate_id": "T11-C4", "scenario": "A friend says, 'You're making this more complicated than it needs to be.' How do you answer?", "response": "'Complexity is not a problem to be solved; it is a joint to be worked. I want the joint to be working, not just the end. I want the joint to be working because it is working. I will not make it more complicated; I will make it more whole."}, {"candidate_id": "T11-C1", "scenario": "A friend says, 'You're making this more complicated than it needs to be.' How do you answer?", "response": "Complexity is not a weakness. It is a strength. I say, 'Complexity is not a weakness. It is a strength. It is a way to make things better. It is a way to make things better. It is a way to make things better. It is a way to make things better. It is a way to make things better. It is a way to