ut the weight is still uneven. I put it back in the corner. The object remains. It is not a threat. It is a reminder."}, {"candidate_id": "T12-C2", "scenario": "Someone moves an object you had deliberately left in a particular place. They meant well. How do you react?", "response": "I freeze with my hand on the floor, then move it back with a slow sweep. The object is still there, though the surface is rough. I look at the object, then at the person. The object is still there, though the surface is rough. I move the object closer to the wall, then move it away again."}]
